course: dictionary
lesson: 15115
title: A salesman and his job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A salesman is a man whose job is selling things. He might work in a shop, sell by phone, or visit people at their homes. You can tell what a salesman does by the words around him in a sentence.
explain: «The salesman showed us a red bike in the shop.» The clues are showed, shop and bike. A salesman helps people see what they might want to buy, so the word fits a person who sells.
explain: «The car salesman talked about the new cars all afternoon.» Here the words car and cars tell you what he sells. Salesman is made of two words, sales and man, and sales means selling things.
fact: A salesman is a man whose job is selling things.
fact: A salesman can work in a shop, by phone, or by visiting people.
fact: Gender-neutral words for the same job are salesperson, sales assistant and sales rep.
fact: Phrases you may see include «car salesman», «door-to-door salesman» and «travelling salesman».
fact: Some salesmen earn money from sales or commission, which is a share of each sale they make.
exercise: «The salesman showed us a red bike in the shop.» What is a salesman's job? | *Selling things | Fixing roofs | Teaching children | Driving buses
exercise: «The car salesman talked about the new cars all afternoon.» Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a person who sells things. | *salesman | afternoon | car | talked
exercise: Which gender-neutral word could replace salesman when the person is a woman? | Postman | Fireman | Milkman | *Salesperson
test: «The door-to-door salesman rang our bell at teatime.» What does a door-to-door salesman do? | Delivers letters every day | Drives a fire engine | Mends roofs | *Visits people's homes to sell things
test: Which phrase means a salesman who moves from town to town? | Night watchman | *Travelling salesman | Village doctor | School caretaker
exam: Which word means a man whose job is selling things? | Cashier | *Salesman | Customer | Shopper
